Mobile landscape lobby looks good, but the deploy button is below the fold (not visible in screenshot) because height 390 and lobby hero scrollable. The weapon cards + deploy may require scroll; on landscape phone, deploy button might be below viewport, but lobby hero has overflow auto. Is it scrollable via touch? Yes, but body touch-action none and lobby-hero overflow auto; touch scrolling may work? CSS `body { touch-action: none; }` could prevent scroll? `touch-action` on body none disables browser panning for descendants unless overridden. `.lobby-hero` no touch-action. This may make scrolling impossible on touch, so deploy button unreachable in landscape. Need ensure deploy visible or lobby hero scroll. Better set `.lobby-hero { touch-action: pan-y; }` and maybe `.lobby-panel` scroll. Also on mobile landscape, reduce vertical spacing to fit deploy. Let's measure: screenshot 390 height, topbar ~57, content from 57 to 390. Game title + stats + cards take most; deploy below. Need compact mobile landscape layout. Could hide map-stats/poi-strip/tagline or reduce. Or move deploy button to fixed bottom? Simpler: for `@media (max-height: 520px) and (pointer: coarse)` hide `.map-stats`, `.poi-strip`, `.tagline`, maybe `.season-tag`, reduce title and card sizes. Then deploy fits.

Let's see screenshot: after topbar, title at 90, tagline 151, stats 176-209, POI 224, loadout title 249, cards 290-380. Deploy would start ~388, out. Need save ~80px. Hide map-stats (~45), poi (~20), tagline (~20), season (~15) = 100. Great. Add:
